{
 "schema": "headroom.circuit.v1",
 "id": "bogner-uberschall-81000",
 "version": 1,
 "name": "Bogner Uberschall (early 2-channel, 4 x EL34, 120 W)",
 "description": "Bogner Uberschall, the early two-channel circuit: V1A input stage into the OC1/OC2 LDR channel switch; Lead channel (P1 gain with C201/C202 bright caps, V1B, V2B, V3A, V3B cathode follower, Marshall-type TMB stack with R70, P6 volume); Clean channel (passive bass network, P7 gain, V4B, treble/mid stack, C310 presence shunt, P12 volume); RE101/K14 channel relay; V5A FX-send cathode follower and the LDR FX loop at rest; V5B recovery and master; 68K/82K LTP phase inverter; 4 x EL34 (folded pairs); NFB from the 4 ohm tap through OC105 (open in Clean) into R121, the presence network and the 0.422 H / 3 uF series resonator; bridge / 470 uF reservoir / choke / 10K-10K-6.8K droppers; -47 V bias with R31 trim.",
 "sources": [
  {
   "title": "'Uberschall', 5/4/2007, REV A, sheets 1/2 (preamp) and 2/2 (power amp), Eagle drawing with measured DC voltages (309/323/383 V rails, every preamp plate and cathode, PI 380/267/269/47.7/46 V, 525 V centre tap, -47 V bias) and the NFB inductor spec; music-electronics-forum attachment 'bogner Uberschall.pdf' (primary source)",
   "url": "https://music-electronics-forum.com/filedata/fetch?id=833076"
  },
  {
   "title": "'Uberschall_preamp.sch', 2012, 2 sheets 'BOGNER UBERSCHALL PREAMP' / 'POWER AMP', marked 'for educational purposes only, may contain topology, component value errors': supply, droppers, bias network, OT taps, channel-relay LED drive (secondary source; disagreements listed in the notes)",
   "url": "https://el34world.com/charts/Schematics/files/Bogner/Uberschall.pdf"
  },
  {
   "title": "N. Koren, 'Improved vacuum tube models for SPICE simulations': 12AX7 and EL34 laws (library models)",
   "url": "https://www.normankoren.com/Audio/Tubemodspice_article.html"
  }
 ],
